```javascript
function houseSquareClick(e) {
  if (gridClickEnabled) {
    var clickedSquare = e.target.feature;

    // Get the bounding box of the clicked square
    var bbox = e.target.getBounds();

    var imageUrl = 'https://cdn.glitch.global/12fb2e80-41df-442d-8bf7-be84a3d85f59/_5bf487a3-e022-43b0-bbbb-29c7d2337032.jpeg?v=1713694179855';
    var latLngBounds = L.latLngBounds([[bbox.getSouth(), bbox.getWest()], [bbox.getNorth(), bbox.getEast()]]);

    var imageOverlay = L.imageOverlay(imageUrl, latLngBounds, {
      opacity: 0.8,
      interactive: true,
      metadata: { squareId: clickedSquare.properties.id } // Add square ID to metadata
    }).addTo(map);

    // Add the image overlay to the array and log the ID
    houseImageOverlays.push(imageOverlay);
    console.log("House image added for square ID:", clickedSquare.properties.id);

    if (houseImageOverlays.length === 4) {
      // Extract the square IDs of the clicked squares
      var squareIds = houseImageOverlays.map(function(overlay) {
        return overlay.options.metadata.squareId;
      });

      // Check for the specific 2x2 grid pattern with IDs 0,1,16,17
      if (
        squareIds.includes(0) &&
        squareIds.includes(1) &&
        squareIds.includes(16) &&
        squareIds.includes(17)
      ) {
        console.log('The four house image overlays form a 2x2 grid pattern.');

        // Remove the four existing overlays from the map
        houseImageOverlays.forEach(function(overlay) {
          map.removeLayer(overlay);
        });

        // Clear the array
        houseImageOverlays = [];

        // Calculate the bounding box that fits all four squares
        // Assuming you have access to the squareGrid array with features and their IDs
        var squaresToCover = squareGrid.filter(function(feature) {
          return [0, 1, 16, 17].includes(feature.properties.id);
        });

        // Get combined bounds
        var combinedBounds = squaresToCover.reduce(function(bounds, feature) {
          var coords = feature.geometry.coordinates[0].map(function(coord) {
            return [coord[1], coord[0]]; // Convert [lng, lat] to [lat, lng]
          });
          var featureBounds = L.latLngBounds(coords);
          return bounds ? bounds.extend(featureBounds) : featureBounds;
        }, null);

        // Add the new image overlay covering all four squares
        var newImageUrl = 'https://cdn.glitch.global/12fb2e80-41df-442c-8bf7-be84a3d85f59/_9db268f2-46e3-442c-9331-03056fe46efa.jpeg?v=1714403188285';
        var newImageOverlay = L.imageOverlay(newImageUrl, combinedBounds, {
          opacity: 0.8,
          interactive: true
        }).addTo(map);

        // Optionally add this new overlay to the array if you want to track it
        houseImageOverlays.push(newImageOverlay);
      } else {
        console.log('The four house image overlays do not form the specified 2x2 grid pattern.');
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This code does the following:
- Checks if the four overlays correspond to the square IDs 0, 1, 16, and 17.
- Removes the existing four overlays from the map and clears the `houseImageOverlays` array.
- Calculates the combined bounding box of the four squares using their coordinates from the `squareGrid` array.
- Adds a new image overlay with the specified URL that covers the combined bounding box.

Make sure that the `squareGrid` variable is accessible in this scope and contains the GeoJSON features with their `properties.id` and coordinates as in your original code.

